From 182f7666e88ded5f048c18e69866a8613d3ec687 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:00:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Stabilize WebView shutdown, navigation history and window
 controls

- WebUi: never block the SDL thread on the WebView thread. start(),
  set_visible() and stop() now pump SDL's Win32 message queue while waiting
  (WebView2 creates/re-parents/destroys a child of the SDL window from its own
  thread and sends messages to the SDL thread, so a plain wait/join can
  deadlock). A stuck WebView thread is detached after 5 s instead of keeping
  the process alive.
- Keep the previously uncommitted fixes: ready-gated duplicate-sync cache,
  focus changes moved out of the WebView thread, WM_QUIT posted to the WebView
  thread on stop, Ctrl+Q honoured while a load is in progress.
- Invalidate the duplicate-sync cache on every WebView event so a rejected
  navigation cannot leave the page out of step with the engine.
- Tabs (TV en vivo, Peliculas, Series, Favoritos) replace the history with
  Inicio instead of stacking, so Back returns to Inicio and the nav bar stays
  consistent with the content.
- Esc / Back at Inicio no longer closes the borderless fullscreen app when the
  WebView UI is active (Ctrl+Q, Alt+F4 and the new close button still exit).
- Web UI: visible fullscreen and close buttons, errors shown in full as a
  toast, status pill truncates with an ellipsis, "sin sesion" counts as error,
  search box keeps a usable minimum width.
- Catalog, authentication, session, service requests and playback sources are
  untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
